A1. After this—a walk back. ~ SLAP
A5. Try these for the long pull. ~ SLEDS
A10. A bare necessity in the Follies. ~ CAST
A14. This is horse play. ~ POLO
A15. What's missing on beach attire. ~ LIMIT
A16. A tree-sitter from 'way back. ~ OMAR
A17. When you do this you feel like swearing. ~ AVER
A18. Any Judge will do this. ~ AMUSE
A19. Synonym for "liberty." ~ RENO
A20. The foot-shifting stage. ~ RESTIVE
A22. Roared (look it up in your big Webster). ~ CROONED
A24. The Cockney idea of location. ~ ERE
A25. Good—she's got to be good. ~ NUN
A26. This gets kicked around in Wall Street; Wall Street football. ~ SHARE
A29. Wide open spaces (singular). ~ GAP
A32. To put the eats in reverse. ~ RETCH
A36. These like water—externally. ~ WETS
A37. A collection of locks and quays. ~ CANAL
A39. This is subject to change without notice. ~ TIRE
